{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T18:41:01Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-152484-en",
  "_rev": "dJ4ZpMyfIFtQ0D7lyxWvJX",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T14:25:04Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Whether you struggle with connectivity in Egypt depends a lot on how the trip is built."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "mxjowt7ov3ez",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a usual trip through "
        },
        {
          "_key": "jq3huv4wzavk",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "y4ixfi42hji0"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "u7fvdp7knfw8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "0w78ukysauhb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "xfqpl20upqn1"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "jqqm4s38thuz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "yq3qz01xthym",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "nncabmmhrlrj"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "724rfkjkvk9z",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "zuxlqmyddabw",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "560hhiw4cglt"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "vq5znpykjsa4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "ob783el0fmyo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "0i0rbi1tyq90"
          ],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        },
        {
          "_key": "32q2fimdpr2y",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and the Red Sea resorts, a local SIM or eSIM covers almost every situation. Ride-hailing apps, maps, WhatsApp, hotel contact, ticket and flight checks."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "y4ixfi42hji0",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "xfqpl20upqn1",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "nncabmmhrlrj",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "560hhiw4cglt",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "0i0rbi1tyq90",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For Siwa, the Western Desert, long Eastern Desert roads, or inland Sinai, plan for coverage to drop."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters isn't which operator is absolutely best. It's deciding in advance which fits — physical SIM, eSIM, or roaming."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt's main operators"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "There are four main mobile operators in Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Vodafone Egypt, Orange Egypt, e& Egypt, and WE. e& Egypt is still sometimes called by its previous name, Etisalat. WE is Telecom Egypt's mobile brand."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "u94xlcp8wc54",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In major cities and tourist areas, all of them generally work. In Cairo, Giza, Luxor, Aswan, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "09prjycfot5z",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "mcckegzsqqs8"
          ],
          "text": "Hurghada"
        },
        {
          "_key": "od13ujvuck1y",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Sharm el-Sheikh, and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "0eadnawgzug4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "f370sl11a7yn"
          ],
          "text": "Dahab"
        },
        {
          "_key": "3cxgspj09qya",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", you shouldn't have major coverage problems."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "mcckegzsqqs8",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "f370sl11a7yn",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-59436",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Differences appear on desert roads and in remote areas. For stability on the move and outside cities, more travellers tend to choose Vodafone. For price and data volume, e& or WE can fit."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "5G launched commercially in Egypt in 2025. For travellers, whether you have 5G matters less than whether 4G is stable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A local SIM is most realistic"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For most travellers, the most practical option is a local SIM bought at the airport or an official city store."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The reason is simple. Cheap, plenty of data, and a local number. Useful too where number verification is needed for ride-hailing or some local services."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "At Cairo International Airport, you can buy tourist SIMs at the main operators' counters. After collecting bags, the stores are usually in easy-to-find places, and staff are used to handling tourists."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What's needed is usually your passport. SIM registration requires ID in Egypt. Not a special arrangement for tourists — it is the registration system for telecommunications contracts."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "After buying, always confirm connectivity on the spot. Insert the SIM. Restart the device. Open a map or browser. Confirm data is moving before leaving the counter. Skip this and you may end up at a city store later."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "eSIM is convenient but tends to cost more"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The advantage of eSIM is being able to prepare before arrival."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For people who don't want to queue at the SIM counter, short stays, and late-night arrivals heading straight to the hotel — convenient. Peace of mind to use ride-hailing or WhatsApp right after landing."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cost tends to be higher than a local SIM. For the same data, international eSIM is often pricier. Not a problem for a few days; for a week or more with heavy map and social use, a local SIM is more cost-effective."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Confirm before departure that your device supports eSIM and is not carrier-locked. Even on supported devices, a remaining carrier lock can block it."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Local-operator eSIMs are expanding too, but for tourists, the physical SIM is still clearer in many situations. If using international eSIM, read the activation method before leaving and have the QR code or app information available offline."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Roaming as a backup"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "International roaming on your home operator works."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Costs run high. Daily-flat plans, slowed data, surcharges — conditions vary by contract. An option for short business trips or people who avoid hassle over cost; for a usual trip, a local SIM or eSIM is more rational."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Roaming works as a backup right after arrival. Until you buy a SIM at the airport, until you reach the hotel, until you open a ride-hailing app. After that, leave the main traffic to local SIM or eSIM to manage cost."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Which to choose"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a week or longer, a local SIM is the easiest. If you arrive in Cairo, buy at the airport and confirm activation there."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For 2 to 3 nights, eSIM is enough. Being usable on arrival can matter more than the price gap."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For people who need to keep a number for work or take calls on a home number, combining roaming and a local data SIM is an option. Many recent smartphones combine physical SIM and eSIM."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For desert or remote travel, don't try to solve safety only through operator choice. Some places lose signal. Save important maps offline, move with trusted drivers or arrangements, and consider satellite devices if needed."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What to confirm when buying"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When buying a SIM, confirm these on the spot."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Data volume. Validity period. Are domestic calls included. Are international calls separate. Are prices tax-inclusive. Is tethering allowed. How to top up."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Tourist SIMs may be sold as \"lots of data,\" but volumes are often split into social, video, and general data. If detailed conditions matter, ask how much general data — usable on any app — is included."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "After payment, keep the receipt or SIM card. They may be needed for number or support enquiries."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Where signal weakens"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Cairo, Giza, Luxor, Aswan, Alexandria, and along the Red Sea, most travellers have no issues."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Signal weakens on long desert roads. The Luxor-Hurghada road, oasis-to-oasis transfers, the road to Siwa, inland Sinai — coverage drops in places."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "On a cruise, signal works in river-side cities and towns; speed varies by location. Don't over-rely on ship Wi-Fi. Even where on-board Wi-Fi is listed, stability depends on boat and section."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hotel Wi-Fi is the same. Even at luxury hotels, signal can be weak depending on room position. For work or important calls, have your own mobile data, not only hotel Wi-Fi."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "From Japan"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Japanese carrier roaming is convenient but tends to run high on longer trips."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To keep a Japanese number, leave the Japanese SIM for voice and SMS reception and use an Egyptian SIM or eSIM for data. For people who need Japanese SMS for banking or two-factor authentication, confirm before departure that your device can run dual-SIM."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To use a local SIM in Egypt, the smartphone must be unlocked. On older devices or carrier-purchased devices, confirm SIM-lock status before leaving."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In sum"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Connectivity for an Egypt trip doesn't need to be overthought."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a usual trip, buy a local SIM at Cairo airport or an official city store and confirm activation on the spot. For short stays or late arrivals, prepare an eSIM in advance. Use roaming as a backup."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "These three patterns are enough for most travellers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters is not panicking after arrival. Buy at an official store with your passport. Confirm connectivity before leaving. In the desert, assume you'll go out of coverage."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "That alone makes transfers, contact, maps, and reservation checks in Egypt considerably easier."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
  "category": {
    "_ref": "wp-category-21",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "deck": "Local SIM, eSIM, or international roaming for Egypt — major operators, airport purchase, passport registration, and where the desert goes out of coverage.",
  "heroImage": {
